# Process-tree guard (required for all test commands)

The rules themselves are in `AGENTS.md` → **Process-Tree Guard**, and the tuning
knobs are in `docs/agent-process-guard.md`. Read those; this rule exists to make
them always-applied in Cursor and to record the one Cursor-specific fact:

- `.cursor/hooks.json` registers `beforeShellExecution` →
  `scripts/guard-agent-command.mjs --protocol=cursor`, which blocks unguarded
  test entrypoints mechanically. Hooks are a recent Cursor feature — if a Cursor
  version does not honor them, the npm scripts are still guarded and only the
  direct-binary bypass reopens, which is why the written rule has to stand on its
  own too.
